---
description: >-
  Label syntax with markdownAlwaysOn (#1368, #1400): the source of label-syntax.mmd with the
  setting on, so every line is markdown and the picture differs from the default one. The one
  effect is written plain here (a quoted markdown string there), so that every label kind shows
  plain markers read as markdown. The
  plain `**bold** _ital_` lines draw bold and italic, bare backticks and the code-span lines draw
  inline code, in the effect, the causes and the sub-causes; a quoted markdown string, tags and
  `\n` draw as in the default mode.
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
---
ishikawa-beta
  effect **bold** _ital_
  cause **bold** _ital_
    sub **bold** _ital_
  "`cause **bold** _ital_`"
    "`sub **bold** _ital_`"
      "`deep **bold** _ital_`"
  `cause **bold** _ital_`
    `sub **bold** _ital_`
  cause a `code` b
    sub a `code` b
  cause <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
    sub <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
  cause one\ntwo
    sub one\ntwo
